            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A bed exercise system (100) comprises a foot pad (120, 1320), a leg support member (122), and first and second elastic connectors (124, 1324; 126, 1326). The foot pad (120, 1320) has a first lateral side (130, 1330), a second lateral side (132, 1332) opposite the first lateral side (130, 1330), an upper side (134), and a lower side (136). The foot pad (120) further comprises a proximal surface (138) and a distal surface (140) opposite the proximal surface (138), wherein the proximal surface (138) and the distal surface (140) extend between the first lateral side (130, 1330), the second lateral side (132, 1332), the upper side (134), and the lower side (136). The proximal surface (138) is configured to engage one or more soles of one or more feet (116) of an operator (104). The foot pad (120, 1320) comprises at least one foot retention structure that is configured to couple the foot pad (120, 1320) to the one or more feet (116) of the operator (104). The leg support member (122) extends proximally from the lower side (136) of the foot pad (120, 1320), wherein the leg support member (122) is configured to support one or more ankles and one or more legs (112) of the operator (104) during operation of the bed exercise system (100). The first elastic connector (124, 1324) has a first end (164) coupled to the first lateral side (130) of the foot pad (120, 1320) and a second end (166) configured to couple to a patient support structure (102). The second elastic connector (126, 1326) has a first end (168) coupled to the second lateral side (132) of the foot pad (120, 1320) and a second end (170) configured to couple to the patient support structure (102). When the second end (166) of the first elastic connector (124, 1324) and the second end (170) of the second elastic connector (126, 1326) are coupled to the patient support structure (102): (i) the foot pad (120) is movable between a first position and a second position relative to the patient support structure (102), and (ii) a tension on the first elastic connector (124, 1324) and a tension on the second elastic connector (126, 1326) increases as the foot pad (120) moves from the first position to the second position.</p>
            </abstract>
